  abstract = {Unidirectional transport and localized cyclotron motion are two opposite physical phenomena. Here, we study the interplay effects between them on nonreciprocal lattices subject to a magnetic field. We show that, in the long-wavelength limit, the trajectories of the wave packets always form closed orbits in four-dimensional complex space. Therefore, the semiclassical quantization rules persist despite the nonreciprocity, which preserves real Landau levels. We predict a different type of non-Hermitian spectral transition induced by the spontaneous breaking of the combined mirror-time reversal ({$MT$}) symmetry, which generally exists in such systems. An order parameter is proposed to describe the {$MT$} phase transition, not only to determine the {$MT$} phase boundary but also to quantify the degree of {$MT$}-symmetry breaking. Such an order parameter can be generally applied to all types of non-Hermitian phase transitions.},
