  abstract = {The finite Berry curvature in topological materials can induce many subtle phenomena, such as anomalous Hall effect (AHE), spin Hall effect (SHE), anomalous Nernst effect (ANE), non-linear Hall effect (NLHE) and bulk photovoltaic effects. To explore these novel physics as well as their connection and coupling, a precise and effective model should be developed. Here, we propose such a versatile model--3D triangular lattice with alternating hopping parameters, which can yield various topological phases, including kagome bands, triply degenerate fermions, double Weyl semimetal and so on. We reveal that this special lattice can present unconventional transport due to its unique topological surface states and the aforementioned topological phenomena, such as the AHE, ANE, NLHE and topological photocurrent effect. In addition, we also provide a number of material candidates that have been synthesized experimentally with this lattice, and discuss two materials including a non-magnetic triangular system for SHE, NLHE and shift current and a ferromagnetic triangular lattice for AHE and ANE. Our work provides an excellent platform including both model and materials for the study of Berry curvature related physics.},
  file = {C\:\\Users\\MrJia\\Zotero\\storage\\8UNDQY9D\\You et al_2023_A versatile model with three-dimensional triangular lattice for unconventional.pdf;C\:\\Users\\MrJia\\Zotero\\storage\\AGAIK57Z\\7143134.html}
}

